# Power tuning for internal rotational HDDs, CachyOS-style: -B 254 sets the
# highest APM level that still allows standby, which stops aggressive head
# parking (constant load/unload cycles); -S 0 disables the spin-down timer.
#
# This is NOT copied verbatim from upstream CachyOS-Settings' 69-hdparm.rules.
# That file has gone through two bugs worth avoiding:
#   - v1.4.0 and earlier: ATTRS{id/bus}=="ata" never matched anything, so
#     the rule was silently a no-op (CachyOS/CachyOS-Settings#268).
#   - v1.4.1's fix (ATTRS{id/bus} -> ENV{ID_BUS}) then also matched
#     USB-bridged SSDs reporting rotational=1 over the uas driver, and
#     hdparm blocked udev for ~21s on those (CachyOS/CachyOS-Settings#274).
# The ENV{ID_USB_DRIVER}=="" clause below is the fix proposed in #274:
# it keeps the rule working for real internal ATA disks while excluding
# anything attached through a USB storage driver.
ACTION=="add|change", KERNEL=="sd[a-z]", ATTR{queue/rotational}=="1", \
    ENV{ID_BUS}=="ata", ENV{ID_USB_DRIVER}=="", RUN+="/usr/sbin/hdparm -B 254 -S 0 /dev/%k"
